{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And he put a veil over his face.</b> As its Targum renders: בֵּית אַפֵּי — it is an Aramaic expression. In the Talmud (Ketubot 62): סְוִי לִבָּהּ; and further in Ketubot (60b): הֲוָה קָא מַסְוֵה לְאַפָּהּ — an expression of looking: he would gaze at her. So too here, מַסְוֶה is a garment placed against the face and the eye-sockets; and for the honor of the beams of radiance — so that all would not feast their eyes on them — he would place the veil against them, and remove it when he spoke with Israel, and when the Omnipresent spoke with him until his going out; and when he went out, he went out without a veil."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:39.500271721Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}